agents — Configure every AI coding harness from one config file

USAGE
  agents [command] [options]

COMMANDS
  init         Write a starter config.toml
  check        Validate the configuration and the native files
  config       Inspect the resolved configuration
  schema       Print the JSON Schema of the configuration
  features     Show which config keys each harness supports
  render       Print the native files apply would write
  apply        Write the native files of every selected harness
  prompt       Edit, show and check instruction layers
  mcp          Manage MCP servers of workspaces
  models       Display model tiers (default) or sync data
  plugins      Inspect, update, or prune plugins
  usage        Show live provider account usage and refresh the cache
  doctor       Advise on models, accounts, and capacity from cached usage
  version      Print version information
  help         Show help for a command path

OPTIONS
  -h, --help
    Show this help and exit.
  -v, --version
    Print version information and exit.

Use agents help <command> for command-specific help.
